From efd27535dc8cf5ad601936415f10fd3dac3162d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob Oursland <jacob.oursland@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 13:33:12 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] Unbundle absl

Use the abseil provided by conda-forge (libabseil-bazel-systemlib) rather than
letting bzlmod fetch and compile abseil from the BCR.

Bazel already links against conda's libgrpc/libprotobuf, but kept building a
vendored abseil for headers. Pinning that vendored copy to the same version as
conda's libabseil (which is what MODULE.bazel's ABSEIL_VERSION placeholder
does) keeps the two ABI-compatible, but it does not make them the same headers:
they still arrive from two different roots. Anything that includes a protobuf
or grpc header and gets abseil transitively then picks up
external/abseil-cpp+/absl/**, which the rule never declared:

    ERROR: external/grpc-java+/compiler/BUILD.bazel:7:10: Compiling
    compiler/src/java_plugin/cpp/java_plugin.cpp [for tool] failed: undeclared
    inclusion(s) in rule '@@grpc-java+//compiler:grpc_java_plugin':
    this rule is missing dependency declarations for the following files
    included by 'compiler/src/java_plugin/cpp/java_plugin.cpp':
      'external/abseil-cpp+/absl/base/attributes.h'
      ...

With the systemlib there is no external/abseil-cpp+ tree at all: the abseil
targets become linkopts, and the headers come from ${PREFIX}/include, which the
generated toolchain already lists as a builtin include directory and which the
strict-header check therefore does not police.

All eleven abseil targets the tree references after patch 0011 are present in
the systemlib, so nothing needs dropping here (unlike 7.x, which also had to
drop absl/utility:if_constexpr).

This mirrors what the main branch does for 9.x and what #299 does for 7.x.
---
 MODULE.bazel | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/MODULE.bazel b/MODULE.bazel
index 1538882..71590f0 100755
--- a/MODULE.bazel
+++ b/MODULE.bazel
@@ -36,6 +36,16 @@ bazel_dep(name = "rules_testing", version = "0.6.0")
 bazel_dep(name = "googletest", version = "1.17.0.bcr.2", repo_name = "com_google_googletest")
 bazel_dep(name = "with_cfg.bzl", version = "0.6.0")
 bazel_dep(name = "abseil-cpp", version = "ABSEIL_VERSION")
+# Use the abseil shipped by conda-forge (via libabseil-bazel-systemlib) instead of
+# letting bzlmod fetch and build a vendored copy. Bazel links against conda's
+# libgrpc/libprotobuf, and the headers those pull in have to be the same abseil;
+# with a bzlmod-built abseil the two meet in third-party compiles that then fail
+# the strict-header check, e.g. @grpc-java//compiler:grpc_java_plugin reporting
+# undeclared inclusions of external/abseil-cpp+/absl/**.
+local_path_override(
+    module_name = "abseil-cpp",
+    path = "./third_party/systemlibs/absl",
+)
 bazel_dep(name = "rules_shell", version = "0.6.1")
 bazel_dep(name = "chicory", version = "1.1.0")
 
